&lt;/ul&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;h3&gt;&lt;strong&gt;About the Role&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Clinical Operations is at the heart of what we do as a healthcare business. As our patient base expands across a growing range of conditions and treatments, we are seeking an experienced Clinical Operations Manager to support the safe and effective scaling of this function.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;In this role, you&#39;ll take charge of our UK prescriber workforce (100+ FTE and rapidly growing) — the clinicians at the core of delivering safe, effective, and world-class care to thousands of patients every day. You&#39;ll ensure they are supported, empowered, and consistently performing at their best. Alongside managing workforce planning and rota design, you&#39;ll drive performance, uphold clinical standards, and embed the systems and oversight that enable scale. This is a pivotal role in building a prescriber function that is both resilient today and ready for the future of digital healthcare.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;You&#39;ll combine people leadership with operational execution, using data and technology to monitor performance, resolve challenges quickly, and identify opportunities to improve safety, efficiency, and patient outcomes. With new clinics and treatments launching in 2025 and beyond, you&#39;ll play a central role in ensuring our prescriber workforce is well-prepared and able to deliver at scale.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;&lt;strong&gt;What You&#39;ll Do&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Lead and Inspire Our Prescriber Workforce - &lt;/strong&gt;Take ownership of the UK prescriber team, driving engagement, setting high standards, and ensuring every clinician is empowered to deliver outstanding patient care with the right tools and tech at their fingertips.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Rota Management &amp;amp; Workforce Planning - &lt;/strong&gt;Own end-to-end rota design, scheduling, and workforce planning for 100+ prescribers. Ensure adequate clinical coverage across all services and time zones, proactively managing demand fluctuations, leave, and growth. Build scalable, automated scheduling systems that maintain safe staffing levels while optimising for cost and clinician experience.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Elevate Performance and Quality at Scale - &lt;/strong&gt;Harness data, automation, and real-time feedback loops to raise the bar on clinical outcomes, ensuring our workforce is consistently safe, effective, and world-class.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Build Systems That Power Growth - &lt;/strong&gt;Design and refine processes that make scheduling, onboarding, and workforce management seamless and scalable, leveraging automation and technology to unlock efficiency and prepare us for future expansion.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Be the Glue Across Teams - &lt;/strong&gt;Partner with Clinical, Operations, Product, and Data leaders to solve problems fast, embed tech-enabled workflows, and launch new services smoothly — creating an environment where prescribers thrive.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;What We Expect From You&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Take accountability for prescriber scheduling, rota management, performance, and development, ensuring care is delivered safely, efficiently, and at scale.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Uphold high clinical standards through clear performance management, audits, and coaching, while balancing commercial goals on efficiency, cost, and conversion.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Bring structure, clarity, and data-driven decision-making to clinical operations, leveraging automation and AI to streamline processes and remove bottlenecks.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Play a key role in rolling out new services across our brands, ensuring prescribers are trained, workflows are ready, and patients receive safe, timely, and effective care from day one.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;&lt;strong&gt;About You&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Skills &amp;amp; Experience&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Operator with clinical depth – &lt;/strong&gt;You bring 5+ years of experience in healthcare operations or clinical management. You may have worked in digital health, a fast-paced startup, consulting, or a tech-enabled healthcare environment.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Built for scale – &lt;/strong&gt;You&#39;ve managed clinical teams or functions in high-growth settings, with proven experience in rota management, shift scheduling, workforce planning, and ensuring safe delivery of care at volume.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Operator&#39;s mindset – &lt;/strong&gt;You move easily between day-to-day execution and process improvement. You&#39;ve led projects that turned complex challenges into streamlined systems and measurable outcomes.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Data fluent – &lt;/strong&gt;You&#39;re confident using clinical and operational data to drive insight, track performance, and implement improvements at pace.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Tech and automation savvy – &lt;/strong&gt;You&#39;ve worked with or implemented tech-enabled workflows, including automation or AI, to improve efficiency, safety, or workforce effectiveness.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Clinically credible (preferred, not essential) – &lt;/strong&gt;You may be a registered clinician (GMC or equivalent), or you&#39;ve worked closely alongside prescribers and multidisciplinary teams, with enough exposure to real-world clinical care to lead with confidence and good judgement.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Behaviours &amp;amp; Attitudes&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Acts like an owner – &lt;/strong&gt;You take full responsibility for workforce and patient outcomes, knowing when to lead from the front and when to empower others to deliver their best work.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Relentlessly patient-first – &lt;/strong&gt;You&#39;re deeply motivated to improve care quality and patient outcomes. You never lose sight of who we serve.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;High standards, low ego – &lt;/strong&gt;You move fast, expect excellence, and stay humble. You give and receive feedback well and lead with accountability.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Systems thinker, clear communicator – &lt;/strong&gt;You distil complexity into clear, actionable plans. You bring others with you through structure and storytelling.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Resilient and focused – &lt;/strong&gt;You thrive in pace and ambiguity. You cut through noise, stay calm under pressure, and get things done.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Curious and impact-driven – &lt;/strong&gt;You challenge how things are done and constantly look for better ways to deliver outcomes at scale.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Why Join Eucalyptus?&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Make a real impact, fast. &lt;/strong&gt;We build in the open together, which helps us learn and iterate more quickly, enabling us to deliver high-quality outcomes faster than anyone else — helping to impact patients&#39; lives for the better from the moment you join.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;You&#39;ll be supported to accelerate your career. &lt;/strong&gt;Regular feedback, alongside our bi-annual performance reviews, a professional development budget, and leave help ensure you have the support you need to level up. We&#39;re committed to helping every Eucalypt reach their full potential.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;You&#39;ll work with others who are incredibly passionate. &lt;/strong&gt;Our talent bar is high, and our work ethic is strong. You&#39;ll get to stretch yourself every day, be given autonomy to tackle interesting problems, and work amongst people who care deeply about our patients.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Benefits&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Your own stake in the business with our employee options programme&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;A monthly wellness allowance, for you to spend on whatever wellness means to you&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;A yearly personal development budget and 3 extra days of leave to continuously up-skill yourself&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;25 days holiday + bank holidays with an enhanced parental leave policy&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;A fun office with regular socials including after-school sport, clubs, cycle kick-offs, and seasonal parties&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Your own MacBook and more!&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;em&gt;Want to hear more about what it&#39;s like to work at Eucalyptus? &lt;/em&gt;&lt;em&gt;Hear from our team&lt;/em&gt;&lt;em&gt; or check us out on Instagram &lt;/em&gt;&lt;em&gt;@eucalyptus.health&lt;/em&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;div class=&quot;content-conclusion&quot;&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;em&gt;At Eucalyptus, we value individuals from all backgrounds, experiences, and perspectives, and we embrace the unique qualities each person brings. When you apply, please let us know of any reasonable adjustments you may need during the interview process. We use AI-assisted tools across our business to help our teams work more efficiently, including within our recruitment process. These tools support our team — all hiring decisions are made by real people, and every application is reviewed by a member of our recruitment team.&lt;/em&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;/div&gt;

f0ee2e84-bcf9-5558-9bad-7ed0b8eafbfb.original_description:
&lt;div class=&quot;content-intro&quot;&gt;&lt;h3&gt;About Eucalyptus&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;p&gt;We&#39;re on a mission to make good health last a lifetime. More than 1 billion people live with obesity worldwide, driving preventable chronic conditions. We&#39;re here to build better long-term care.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Eucalyptus is now part of Hims &amp;amp; Hers, the global leader in personalised health and wellness.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Euc is the company behind Juniper, one of the world&#39;s largest weight-management programs combining GLP-1 medication with personalised nutrition, movement support, and clinician-led care from prescribers, nurses, health coaches, pharmacists, and dietitians. Our published clinical research shows that our combined clinical and behavioural approach helps patients lose significantly more weight during their treatment with Juniper by four times.&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;Our Growth Story:&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Supporting patients living with obesity across our 5 markets&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Received selective NICE endorsement to provide services to the NHS&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Tailored our offering to thousands of patients in Australia, the UK, Germany, Japan and Canada.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;h3&gt;About the Role&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;p&gt;We are looking for a &lt;strong&gt;Clinical Quality Analyst&lt;/strong&gt; to safeguard the clinical quality of every patient-facing Medical Support interaction at Eucalyptus. Our Medical Support teams handle some of the most sensitive conversations in the business — severe side effects, hospitalisations, mental health presentations, eligibility decisions, and patients who are not seeing results. This role exists to make sure those conversations are consistently safe, accurate, empathetic, and clinically sound as we scale across markets.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;You will audit interactions across phone, email, and chat through both a patient-first and a clinical-safety lens; own the clinical scoring framework and keep it calibrated and trusted; and turn what you find into coaching recommendations, macro and workflow corrections, and training that measurably improves care. When you find a clinical risk, you will escalate it — quickly, clearly, and without waiting for a reporting cycle.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;This is a role for someone who has worked clinically and then found they were drawn to the systems question: not just &lt;em&gt;was this patient looked after&lt;/em&gt;, but &lt;em&gt;why did this go wrong, how often, and what needs to change&lt;/em&gt;. You might come from clinical governance, safety and quality audit, incident review, accreditation, or a clinical QA function in a hospital, pharmacy, or health service — or you might be a clinician who has been doing this work informally and wants to do it properly. This role reports to the Manager, Quality, Training &amp;amp; Process Excellence and sits deliberately outside the teams it audits.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;If you are clinically sharp, rigorous about evidence, comfortable telling people what you found, and motivated by making care measurably safer at scale — this role is for you.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;hr&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;What You&#39;ll Be Doing&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Clinical Quality Auditing&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Audit patient-facing Medical Support interactions across phone, email, and chat — escalation, discovery, eligibility and Medical Support calls, side-effect queues, pre-approvals, and formal patient check-ins&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Assess both experience quality (tone, empathy, clarity, de-escalation) and clinical quality (accuracy of information, appropriateness of advice, safety-netting, documentation, escalation decisions)&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Deliver audit coverage at a frequency and sample design that is genuinely representative across every channel, queue, and team member&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Maintain audit documentation that is complete, defensible, and stands up to regulatory scrutiny&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Scoring Framework &amp;amp; Calibration&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Own and improve the clinical QA scoring framework, including clinical criteria, weightings, and the definition of a critical clinical error&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Run calibration sessions with Team Leads, Senior Medical Support Associates, and clinical stakeholders so scoring stays consistent and trusted&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Keep the framework aligned to current clinical protocols, formulary, and market-specific regulatory requirements&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Clinical Risk Identification &amp;amp; Escalation&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Identify clinical risks, recurring errors, and emerging unsafe patterns, and escalate them through the defined clinical escalation path&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Distinguish clearly between a coaching moment, a systemic quality issue, and a reportable clinical safety event — and act on each correctly&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Partner with Clinical Operations and Clinical Insights on any finding indicating patient harm, a near-miss, or a protocol gap&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;QA Reporting &amp;amp; Insight&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Produce weekly clinical QA reporting covering scores, trends, clinical error themes, and specific coaching and training recommendations&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Analyse QA results alongside ticket quality, error rates, escalation volumes, patient satisfaction, and clinical incident data to surface patterns worth acting on&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Make reporting insight-led — a narrative that tells stakeholders what to focus on and why&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Clinical Content Assurance&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Review and maintain Medical Support macros, templates, and workflows so the clinical content within them stays accurate, current, and compliant across markets&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Drive correction of anything clinically out of date or unsafe, confirming the right clinical position with Clinical Operations&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Partner with Process &amp;amp; Knowledge Specialists so approved changes land in the Knowledge Hub and in training, not just in the macro library&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Training &amp;amp; Coaching Partnership&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Partner with Learning &amp;amp; Knowledge Management to design and deliver clinical training that closes the specific gaps your audits reveal&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Provide structured, specific, evidence-grounded coaching recommendations to Team Leads&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Measure training impact through subsequent QA outcomes and knowledge checks, and iterate on what the evidence shows&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Process Improvement &amp;amp; Automation&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Bring clinical QA data into process and automation discussions so clinical safety is designed in, not reviewed afterwards&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Collaborate with Process Specialists and Senior Medical Support Associates to close gaps and improve turnaround times without eroding clinical quality&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Track and report the clinical quality impact of every change implemented&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Cross-Functional Collaboration &amp;amp; Patient Insight&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Capture and synthesise clinical patient insight, sentiment trends, and safety themes from the frontline&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Share findings proactively with Operations, Clinical Operations, Product, and Care partners to inform improvements&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Ensure both the patient voice and the clinical view are represented in quality, process, and product discussions&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;hr&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;About You&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;3–5 years&lt;/strong&gt; of post-qualification clinical experience, with at least &lt;strong&gt;2 years&lt;/strong&gt; in a clinical quality, clinical governance, safety and quality, audit, accreditation, or incident review capacity — telehealth or a fast-paced healthcare environment is a strong plus&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;A clinical qualification and background&lt;/strong&gt; — registered nurse, midwife, pharmacist, paramedic, or allied health professional. You have practised, and you bring real clinical judgement rather than a checklist&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Experience auditing clinical care or clinical documentation&lt;/strong&gt; — you have reviewed cases against a standard, formed a view, and defended it. Experience with adverse event review, root cause analysis, or accreditation frameworks is highly valued&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Analytically capable&lt;/strong&gt; — you turn a pattern across fifty audits into a clear, evidenced recommendation. Comfortable in spreadsheets and reporting tools; SQL or dashboard experience is a bonus, not a requirement&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Rigorous and detail-oriented&lt;/strong&gt; — you notice the missing safety-net, the undocumented escalation, the advice that was almost right&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Direct and constructive&lt;/strong&gt; — you can tell a Team Lead their team has a clinical accuracy problem, and be thanked for it. You separate the finding from the person, and you make feedback specific, fair, and actionable&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Sound judgement on risk&lt;/strong&gt; — you know the difference between a coaching moment and a safety event, and you escalate urgent findings immediately rather than holding them for a report&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Independent and self-directed&lt;/strong&gt; — you design your own audit plan, hold yourself to your own coverage targets, and do not need to be chased&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;A genuine collaborator&lt;/strong&gt; — you work generously across Medical Support, Clinical Operations, Learning, and Process teams, and you share what you find early&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Patient-first in everything&lt;/strong&gt; — every audit, score, and recommendation is anchored in what is safest and best for the patient&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Based in Metro Manila and happy to join us at our Makati hub 2–3 days per week as part of our hybrid working model, working hours aligned to our AU and UK teams&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;hr&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Why Join Eucalyptus?&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Euc is also behind a growing family of digital healthcare clinics (&lt;a href=&quot;https://pilot.com.au/&quot;&gt;Pilot,&lt;/a&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;a href=&quot;http://www.kinfertility.com.au/&quot;&gt;Kin&lt;/a&gt;,&amp;nbsp;&lt;a href=&quot;http://skin.software/&quot;&gt;Software&lt;/a&gt;, &lt;a href=&quot;https://www.compound.co/&quot;&gt;Compound&lt;/a&gt;) across men’s health and well-being, fertility, skincare, and preventative health.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Here’s what makes joining Euc unique:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;What’s next&lt;/strong&gt; - Our goal for the next three years is to support &lt;strong&gt;1 million patients globally&lt;/strong&gt; to live better for longer. We’re launching into new conditions, demographics, and geographies as we build a truly preventive healthcare ecosystem.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Build something world-changing&lt;/strong&gt; - We’re on the path to becoming the world’s largest international digital healthcare company. It will be challenging, fast-paced, and deeply rewarding.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Make real impact&lt;/strong&gt; - You will deliver work that directly shapes patient outcomes and scales evidence-based care across markets.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Accelerate your growth&lt;/strong&gt; - You will have high ownership, continuous feedback, and dedicated development support.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Join a motivated team&lt;/strong&gt; - You will collaborate with talented peers to solve complex clinical and operational problems at scale.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;hr&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;&lt;strong&gt;What’s Ahead in the Philippines?&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Grow with us globally -&lt;/strong&gt; Get mentorship from leaders across Australia, the UK, Germany, and Japan while collaborating with top-tier teams in the Philippines and South Africa.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Shape your career&lt;/strong&gt; - Access learning budgets, conferences, certifications, peer shadowing, and a global knowledge-sharing culture.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Work where wellbeing matters&lt;/strong&gt; - Enjoy wellness budgets, social clubs, hybrid work arrangement, and initiatives that help you stay balanced and connected.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Innovate with purpose&lt;/strong&gt; - Use state-of-the-art tools and contribute to bold, impactful solutions in healthcare.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Support at every stage&lt;/strong&gt; - Benefit from comprehensive health coverage (including up to 2 dependents), vacation, sick, and parental leaves, 13th-month pay, statutory benefits, and transport allowance.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;em&gt;At Eucalyptus, we value individuals from all backgrounds, experiences, and perspectives, and we embrace the unique qualities each person brings. When you apply, please let us know of any reasonable adjustments you may need during the interview process.&lt;/em&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;div class=&quot;content-conclusion&quot;&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;em&gt;At Eucalyptus, we value individuals from all backgrounds, experiences, and perspectives, and we embrace the unique qualities each person brings. When you apply, please let us know of any reasonable adjustments you may need during the interview process. We use AI-assisted tools across our business to help our teams work more efficiently, including within our recruitment process. These tools support our team — all hiring decisions are made by real people, and every application is reviewed by a member of our recruitment team.&lt;/em&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;/div&gt;

