&lt;p&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Euc is the company behind Juniper, one of the world&#39;s largest weight-management programs combining GLP-1 medication with personalised nutrition, movement support, and clinician-led care from prescribers, nurses, health coaches, pharmacists, and dietitians. Our published clinical research shows that our combined clinical and behavioural approach helps patients lose significantly more weight during their treatment with Juniper by four times.&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;Our Growth Story:&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Supporting patients living with obesity across our 5 markets&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Received selective NICE endorsement to provide services to the NHS&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Tailored our offering to thousands of patients in Australia, the UK, Germany, Japan and Canada.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;h3&gt;&lt;strong&gt;About the role (What you&#39;ll be doing)&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;p&gt;As a Community Support Associate, you&#39;ll play a key role in maintaining a safe, supportive, and high-trust environment for our customers across the Hims and Hers Weight Loss Private Facebook groups. Working closely with the Community and CX teams, you&#39;ll own day-to-day moderation activity across our coverage window — keeping conversations healthy, engaging members, and helping the community run smoothly.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Your core responsibilities:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;This is a fast-paced, operational role that requires sound judgment, attention to detail, and empathy. You&#39;ll help keep our communities safe, supportive, and running smoothly by:&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Reviewing and approving member join requests, verifying eligibility before granting access&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Reviewing and approving member posts before they go live, ensuring they meet community guidelines&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Monitoring posts, comments, and moderation alerts throughout your shift, actively engaging with members and keeping conversations healthy&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Responding to routine questions, directing members to the right resources, and escalating CX issues (billing, shipping, prescriptions, etc.) when needed&lt;/li&gt;
