&lt;div class=&quot;content-intro&quot;&gt;&lt;h3&gt;About Eucalyptus&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;p&gt;We&#39;re on a mission to make good health last a lifetime. More than 1 billion people live with obesity worldwide, driving preventable chronic conditions. We&#39;re here to build better long-term care.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Eucalyptus is now part of Hims &amp;amp; Hers, the global leader in personalised health and wellness.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Euc is the company behind Juniper, one of the world&#39;s largest weight-management programs combining GLP-1 medication with personalised nutrition, movement support, and clinician-led care from prescribers, nurses, health coaches, pharmacists, and dietitians. Our published clinical research shows that our combined clinical and behavioural approach helps patients lose significantly more weight during their treatment with Juniper by four times.&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;Our Growth Story:&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Supporting patients living with obesity across our 5 markets&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Received selective NICE endorsement to provide services to the NHS&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Tailored our offering to thousands of patients in Australia, the UK, Germany, Japan and Canada.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;h3&gt;&lt;strong&gt;About the role (What you’ll be doing)&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;p&gt;The Team Lead is the operational and human heart of the Manila support teams. This role exists to ensure that every agent under their care has the guidance, structure, and support needed to deliver outstanding patient interactions — consistently, safely, and at pace. The Team Lead is equally a people manager, a performance driver, a cultural anchor, and an operational problem solver. They are the first person their team turns to when things get complex, and the person leadership turns to when they need visibility on what is happening on the ground. This role requires someone who leads with empathy and holds with accountability — in equal measure.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;Key Responsibilities&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;h4&gt;1. Team Management &amp;amp; Daily Operations&lt;/h4&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Run daily stand-ups to align the team on ticket handling strategy, priorities, blockers, and important updates — ensuring every agent starts the day informed and focused&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Monitor all queues, assign tickets to agents, and manage workload balance across the team — including backlog management and cross-team absorption where needed&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Act as the first point of support for all agents — approachable, responsive, and genuinely invested in helping the team succeed&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Collaborate actively with other Team Leads to discuss blockers, trends, and insights, and to support each other in delivering consistently strong team lead performance&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h4&gt;2. Performance Management &amp;amp; Agent Development&lt;/h4&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Conduct weekly 1:1 performance reviews with each agent, providing structured feedback, coaching, and a genuine listening ear&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Prepare for each 1:1 proactively, including discussion with the QA analyst to ensure feedback is grounded in both quantitative and qualitative insight&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Hold agents accountable to defined KPIs with fairness, clarity, and consistency&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Identify underperformance early, design and execute relevant performance improvement plans, and escalate material performance issues to the Service Delivery Lead with clear documentation and recommendations&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Foster an environment of psychological and emotional safety where agents feel confident to raise concerns, ask questions, and grow&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h4&gt;3. Reporting &amp;amp; Data Analysis&lt;/h4&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Own, lead, and perform data analysis and reporting at agent, team, and function level&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Track and report on all key metrics as defined with the Service Delivery Lead, providing both quantitative figures and qualitative context&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Prepare weekly, monthly, and cycle reports — each including a clear status against targets and SLAs, and a concrete action plan to address any shortfalls&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Proactively extract and share insights from CSAT data, identifying patterns and root causes rather than just reporting numbers&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Provide each agent with a weekly individual performance report covering both quantitative results and qualitative feedback including CSAT reasons&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Identify and report cross-functional trends and insights to relevant stakeholders&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h4&gt;4. Recurrent Meetings &amp;amp; Stakeholder Engagement&lt;/h4&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Attend, prepare for, and actively contribute to all recurring meetings including Patient Ops Weekly Priorities, PX/MS Weekly Process Updates, and 1:1s with the Service Delivery Lead&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Come to every meeting with a point of view — prepared, engaged, and ready to contribute meaningfully&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h4&gt;5. Escalation Management&lt;/h4&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Act as the escalation point for complex or sensitive patient situations before they are handed off to the escalation team or Senior Associate&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Assess escalations quickly and accurately, resolving independently where within scope and escalating further when required&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Communicate escalation situations proactively and efficiently to relevant stakeholders, supported by clear and concise data&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h4&gt;6. Ad-Hoc &amp;amp; Operational Tasks&lt;/h4&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Manage ad-hoc tasks as they arise including hiring support, PIP management, and specific issue follow-up&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Approach unplanned work with flexibility and ownership — ad-hoc does not mean unstructured, and every task is handled with the same rigor as planned work&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h4&gt;7. Culture &amp;amp; Team Engagement&lt;/h4&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Act as a Culture Champion — embodying Euc&#39;s values and cycle principles in every interaction and decision&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Lead with empathy, care, and understanding while setting a high standard of professionalism across the team&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Ensure agents respect and adopt new ways of working, supporting transitions with clarity and positivity&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Partner with the People team and Senior Associates to organize social initiatives and team events that foster togetherness and a patient-first mentality&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Be a positive energy setter — the kind of leader whose presence raises the standard and the mood of the room&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h4&gt;8. Innovation &amp;amp; Process Improvement&lt;/h4&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Own and drive process improvement initiatives within the team, working closely with Senior Associates to identify gaps and frame practical solutions&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Act as a change champion — embracing new ways of working and advocating for them with energy and conviction&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Build business cases and supporting reports to advocate for improvements and bring them to the attention of the Service Delivery Lead&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Continuously look for innovation opportunities that make the team faster, better, and more patient-focused&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;&lt;strong&gt;About you (Who you are)&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Strong Leader&lt;/strong&gt;: At least 4 years of full-time leadership experience in a startup, international, or tech company. You lead with empathy and kindness while holding your team accountable to high standards. You’ve successfully driven improvements in team performance (CSAT, QA, retention, or efficiency) and fostered a positive team culture. You coach, mentor, and empower team members to grow in their roles.
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Preferably experienced with online/remote/virtual work (not essential).&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Tech-Savvy&lt;/strong&gt;: Proficient in Google Suite (Gmail, Calendar, Drive, Docs, Sheets, Forms, Slides), Slack, Notion, and other productivity/project management tools. Quick to adapt to new systems and technologies. Having experience in Zendesk is a huge plus.&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Strong Communicator&lt;/strong&gt;: Excellent command of English, both spoken and written. You listen attentively and communicate with stakeholders in a concise and effective manner.
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience in healthcare support or a customer-facing role is a plus.&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;People Person&lt;/strong&gt;: Motivates others toward common goals, works well with diverse personalities, and creates an inclusive, psychologically safe environment where people feel heard and valued.&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Exceptional Problem-Solver&lt;/strong&gt;: Approaches complex challenges with creativity and critical thinking. Troubleshoots effectively, resolves technical/operational issues, and knows when to ask clarifying questions. You balance being hands-on in day-to-day operations with providing strategic input to leadership. You thrive in a mission-driven, fast-growing environment and believe in putting patients/customers first.&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Progressive Thinker:&lt;/strong&gt; You don’t just put out fires — you look for root causes and systemic fixes. You use data, feedback loops, and cross-functional collaboration to improve processes at scale. You’re progressive in your approach, anticipating future challenges and opportunities instead of only reacting to the present.&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Ethical Leader&lt;/strong&gt;: Known for integrity and discretion, with the courage to challenge gossip, exclusion, or toxic behaviours. You set a high ethical standard, fostering a culture of trust, accountability, and psychological safety.&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Proactive&lt;/strong&gt;: A charismatic “can-do” attitude with minimal need for supervision. Takes ownership, goes the extra mile, and is motivated by impact and helping others.&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Learner’s Mindset&lt;/strong&gt;: Embraces challenges as learning opportunities. Adapts quickly in fast-paced environments, strives for excellence, and continuously improves. You thrive in a mission-driven, fast-growing environment and view challenges as opportunities to learn. This role also offers growth opportunities into broader leadership areas such as operations, strategy, or project management.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;You are willing to work full-time (40 hours/week) in a hybrid set up during either APAC customer hours
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;APAC Business Hours: 6:00AM - 6:00PM Manila Time&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;You are located near or within Metro Manila, Philippines&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;You have a suitable work-from-home space (work desk, comfortable chair, proper lighting, quiet environment)&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;You have stable internet connection at home: 30 Mbps minimum&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Why you should join Euc&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Our teams are incredibly passionate&lt;/strong&gt; - Our talent bar is high and our work ethic is strong. You’ll get to stretch yourself everyday and work amongst people who care deeply about our patients. You’ll be given autonomy to tackle interesting problems and receive regular feedback from a supportive team&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;We’ll have your back when you need us the most&lt;/strong&gt; - You’ll be able to lean on a range of leave offerings to support you when needed from Day 1, this includes: sick, maternal/paternal, compassionate, and vacation leave. Personal health days leave and budget to encourage you to take care of your well-being. A reliable health insurance provider accredited by major hospitals, clinics, and diagnostic centers nationwide, plus coverage of up to two dependents. Standard employer share for statutory benefits (SSS, PhilHealth, and HDMF), and 13th month pay. Also, transportation allowance to support your expenses when reporting to our Makati office.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;We will invest in your career&lt;/strong&gt; - You’ll get access to an annual professional development budget and additional leave credits, mentors and buddies to ensure that you have the support you need to level up. You can expect regular performance and pay reviews as your career grows.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;We move at incredible speed&lt;/strong&gt; - You’ll work with team mates who build in the open by sharing their work freely, this helps us learn and iterate quickly so we can deliver high quality outcomes faster than our competitors. You’ll **spend a lot of time outside of your comfort zone learning and iterating frequently, we wouldn’t have it any other way&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;div class=&quot;content-conclusion&quot;&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;em&gt;At Eucalyptus, we value individuals from all backgrounds, experiences, and perspectives, and we embrace the unique qualities each person brings. When you apply, please let us know of any reasonable adjustments you may need during the interview process. We use AI-assisted tools across our business to help our teams work more efficiently, including within our recruitment process. These tools support our team — all hiring decisions are made by real people, and every application is reviewed by a member of our recruitment team.&lt;/em&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;/div&gt;

parsed.original_description:
&lt;div class=&quot;content-intro&quot;&gt;&lt;h3&gt;About Eucalyptus&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;p&gt;We&#39;re on a mission to make good health last a lifetime. More than 1 billion people live with obesity worldwide, driving preventable chronic conditions. We&#39;re here to build better long-term care.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Eucalyptus is now part of Hims &amp;amp; Hers, the global leader in personalised health and wellness.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Euc is the company behind Juniper, one of the world&#39;s largest weight-management programs combining GLP-1 medication with personalised nutrition, movement support, and clinician-led care from prescribers, nurses, health coaches, pharmacists, and dietitians. Our published clinical research shows that our combined clinical and behavioural approach helps patients lose significantly more weight during their treatment with Juniper by four times.&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;Our Growth Story:&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Supporting patients living with obesity across our 5 markets&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Received selective NICE endorsement to provide services to the NHS&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Tailored our offering to thousands of patients in Australia, the UK, Germany, Japan and Canada.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;h3&gt;&lt;strong&gt;About the role (What you’ll be doing)&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;p&gt;The Team Lead is the operational and human heart of the Manila support teams. This role exists to ensure that every agent under their care has the guidance, structure, and support needed to deliver outstanding patient interactions — consistently, safely, and at pace. The Team Lead is equally a people manager, a performance driver, a cultural anchor, and an operational problem solver. They are the first person their team turns to when things get complex, and the person leadership turns to when they need visibility on what is happening on the ground. This role requires someone who leads with empathy and holds with accountability — in equal measure.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;Key Responsibilities&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;h4&gt;1. Team Management &amp;amp; Daily Operations&lt;/h4&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Run daily stand-ups to align the team on ticket handling strategy, priorities, blockers, and important updates — ensuring every agent starts the day informed and focused&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Monitor all queues, assign tickets to agents, and manage workload balance across the team — including backlog management and cross-team absorption where needed&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Act as the first point of support for all agents — approachable, responsive, and genuinely invested in helping the team succeed&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Collaborate actively with other Team Leads to discuss blockers, trends, and insights, and to support each other in delivering consistently strong team lead performance&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h4&gt;2. Performance Management &amp;amp; Agent Development&lt;/h4&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Conduct weekly 1:1 performance reviews with each agent, providing structured feedback, coaching, and a genuine listening ear&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Prepare for each 1:1 proactively, including discussion with the QA analyst to ensure feedback is grounded in both quantitative and qualitative insight&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Hold agents accountable to defined KPIs with fairness, clarity, and consistency&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Identify underperformance early, design and execute relevant performance improvement plans, and escalate material performance issues to the Service Delivery Lead with clear documentation and recommendations&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Foster an environment of psychological and emotional safety where agents feel confident to raise concerns, ask questions, and grow&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h4&gt;3. Reporting &amp;amp; Data Analysis&lt;/h4&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Own, lead, and perform data analysis and reporting at agent, team, and function level&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Track and report on all key metrics as defined with the Service Delivery Lead, providing both quantitative figures and qualitative context&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Prepare weekly, monthly, and cycle reports — each including a clear status against targets and SLAs, and a concrete action plan to address any shortfalls&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Proactively extract and share insights from CSAT data, identifying patterns and root causes rather than just reporting numbers&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Provide each agent with a weekly individual performance report covering both quantitative results and qualitative feedback including CSAT reasons&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Identify and report cross-functional trends and insights to relevant stakeholders&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h4&gt;4. Recurrent Meetings &amp;amp; Stakeholder Engagement&lt;/h4&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Attend, prepare for, and actively contribute to all recurring meetings including Patient Ops Weekly Priorities, PX/MS Weekly Process Updates, and 1:1s with the Service Delivery Lead&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Come to every meeting with a point of view — prepared, engaged, and ready to contribute meaningfully&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h4&gt;5. Escalation Management&lt;/h4&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Act as the escalation point for complex or sensitive patient situations before they are handed off to the escalation team or Senior Associate&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Assess escalations quickly and accurately, resolving independently where within scope and escalating further when required&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Communicate escalation situations proactively and efficiently to relevant stakeholders, supported by clear and concise data&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h4&gt;6. Ad-Hoc &amp;amp; Operational Tasks&lt;/h4&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Manage ad-hoc tasks as they arise including hiring support, PIP management, and specific issue follow-up&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Approach unplanned work with flexibility and ownership — ad-hoc does not mean unstructured, and every task is handled with the same rigor as planned work&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h4&gt;7. Culture &amp;amp; Team Engagement&lt;/h4&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Act as a Culture Champion — embodying Euc&#39;s values and cycle principles in every interaction and decision&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Lead with empathy, care, and understanding while setting a high standard of professionalism across the team&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Ensure agents respect and adopt new ways of working, supporting transitions with clarity and positivity&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Partner with the People team and Senior Associates to organize social initiatives and team events that foster togetherness and a patient-first mentality&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Be a positive energy setter — the kind of leader whose presence raises the standard and the mood of the room&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h4&gt;8. Innovation &amp;amp; Process Improvement&lt;/h4&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Own and drive process improvement initiatives within the team, working closely with Senior Associates to identify gaps and frame practical solutions&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Act as a change champion — embracing new ways of working and advocating for them with energy and conviction&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Build business cases and supporting reports to advocate for improvements and bring them to the attention of the Service Delivery Lead&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Continuously look for innovation opportunities that make the team faster, better, and more patient-focused&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;&lt;strong&gt;About you (Who you are)&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Strong Leader&lt;/strong&gt;: At least 4 years of full-time leadership experience in a startup, international, or tech company. You lead with empathy and kindness while holding your team accountable to high standards. You’ve successfully driven improvements in team performance (CSAT, QA, retention, or efficiency) and fostered a positive team culture. You coach, mentor, and empower team members to grow in their roles.
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Preferably experienced with online/remote/virtual work (not essential).&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Tech-Savvy&lt;/strong&gt;: Proficient in Google Suite (Gmail, Calendar, Drive, Docs, Sheets, Forms, Slides), Slack, Notion, and other productivity/project management tools. Quick to adapt to new systems and technologies. Having experience in Zendesk is a huge plus.&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Strong Communicator&lt;/strong&gt;: Excellent command of English, both spoken and written. You listen attentively and communicate with stakeholders in a concise and effective manner.
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience in healthcare support or a customer-facing role is a plus.&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;People Person&lt;/strong&gt;: Motivates others toward common goals, works well with diverse personalities, and creates an inclusive, psychologically safe environment where people feel heard and valued.&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Exceptional Problem-Solver&lt;/strong&gt;: Approaches complex challenges with creativity and critical thinking. Troubleshoots effectively, resolves technical/operational issues, and knows when to ask clarifying questions. You balance being hands-on in day-to-day operations with providing strategic input to leadership. You thrive in a mission-driven, fast-growing environment and believe in putting patients/customers first.&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Progressive Thinker:&lt;/strong&gt; You don’t just put out fires — you look for root causes and systemic fixes. You use data, feedback loops, and cross-functional collaboration to improve processes at scale. You’re progressive in your approach, anticipating future challenges and opportunities instead of only reacting to the present.&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Ethical Leader&lt;/strong&gt;: Known for integrity and discretion, with the courage to challenge gossip, exclusion, or toxic behaviours. You set a high ethical standard, fostering a culture of trust, accountability, and psychological safety.&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Proactive&lt;/strong&gt;: A charismatic “can-do” attitude with minimal need for supervision. Takes ownership, goes the extra mile, and is motivated by impact and helping others.&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Learner’s Mindset&lt;/strong&gt;: Embraces challenges as learning opportunities. Adapts quickly in fast-paced environments, strives for excellence, and continuously improves. You thrive in a mission-driven, fast-growing environment and view challenges as opportunities to learn. This role also offers growth opportunities into broader leadership areas such as operations, strategy, or project management.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;You are willing to work full-time (40 hours/week) in a hybrid set up during either APAC customer hours
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;APAC Business Hours: 6:00AM - 6:00PM Manila Time&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;You are located near or within Metro Manila, Philippines&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;You have a suitable work-from-home space (work desk, comfortable chair, proper lighting, quiet environment)&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;You have stable internet connection at home: 30 Mbps minimum&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Why you should join Euc&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Our teams are incredibly passionate&lt;/strong&gt; - Our talent bar is high and our work ethic is strong. You’ll get to stretch yourself everyday and work amongst people who care deeply about our patients. You’ll be given autonomy to tackle interesting problems and receive regular feedback from a supportive team&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;We’ll have your back when you need us the most&lt;/strong&gt; - You’ll be able to lean on a range of leave offerings to support you when needed from Day 1, this includes: sick, maternal/paternal, compassionate, and vacation leave. Personal health days leave and budget to encourage you to take care of your well-being. A reliable health insurance provider accredited by major hospitals, clinics, and diagnostic centers nationwide, plus coverage of up to two dependents. Standard employer share for statutory benefits (SSS, PhilHealth, and HDMF), and 13th month pay. Also, transportation allowance to support your expenses when reporting to our Makati office.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;We will invest in your career&lt;/strong&gt; - You’ll get access to an annual professional development budget and additional leave credits, mentors and buddies to ensure that you have the support you need to level up. You can expect regular performance and pay reviews as your career grows.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;We move at incredible speed&lt;/strong&gt; - You’ll work with team mates who build in the open by sharing their work freely, this helps us learn and iterate quickly so we can deliver high quality outcomes faster than our competitors. You’ll **spend a lot of time outside of your comfort zone learning and iterating frequently, we wouldn’t have it any other way&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;div class=&quot;content-conclusion&quot;&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;em&gt;At Eucalyptus, we value individuals from all backgrounds, experiences, and perspectives, and we embrace the unique qualities each person brings. When you apply, please let us know of any reasonable adjustments you may need during the interview process. We use AI-assisted tools across our business to help our teams work more efficiently, including within our recruitment process. These tools support our team — all hiring decisions are made by real people, and every application is reviewed by a member of our recruitment team.&lt;/em&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;/div&gt;

51e112c9-c219-5dd3-adf5-c7c591c08220.original_description:
&lt;div class=&quot;content-intro&quot;&gt;&lt;h3&gt;About Eucalyptus&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;p&gt;We&#39;re on a mission to make good health last a lifetime. More than 1 billion people live with obesity worldwide, driving preventable chronic conditions. We&#39;re here to build better long-term care.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Eucalyptus is now part of Hims &amp;amp; Hers, the global leader in personalised health and wellness.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Euc is the company behind Juniper, one of the world&#39;s largest weight-management programs combining GLP-1 medication with personalised nutrition, movement support, and clinician-led care from prescribers, nurses, health coaches, pharmacists, and dietitians. Our published clinical research shows that our combined clinical and behavioural approach helps patients lose significantly more weight during their treatment with Juniper by four times.&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;Our Growth Story:&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Supporting patients living with obesity across our 5 markets&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Received selective NICE endorsement to provide services to the NHS&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Tailored our offering to thousands of patients in Australia, the UK, Germany, Japan and Canada.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;h3&gt;&lt;strong&gt;The role&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;div&gt;We&#39;re looking for a Creative Producer with a strong Art Director streak. You own the &lt;em&gt;make&lt;/em&gt; end-to-end — concept, look, shoot, edit — but the emphasis here is on &lt;strong&gt;craft and visual direction&lt;/strong&gt;: you&#39;re the person who decides how the work looks and feels, sets the bar, and makes sure every asset that leaves the studio is something we&#39;re proud to put spend behind.&lt;br&gt;You&#39;ll concept and art-direct performance creative that beats the agency benchmark, then produce it — running the shoot, directing talent and the bench, and steering the edit. Your masters become the &quot;gold standard&quot; the rest of the pipeline expands into hundreds of variations, so the quality of your output sets the ceiling for everything.&lt;br&gt;This is a hands-on, high-output role for a swiss-army-knife operator: equal parts taste, ideas and get-it-done.&lt;br&gt;What you&#39;ll do&lt;/div&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Own the visual craft and direction&lt;/strong&gt; of Weight Loss creative — art-direct the look, feel, and quality bar across video and static.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Concept performance-led ideas rooted in what actually works — hooks, angles, formats — not just what looks nice.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Produce end-to-end: plan and run shoots, direct talent and our on-camera bench, and steer edits to a finished standard.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Set the &quot;gold standard&quot; masters that the Manila team and AI iterate and expand from — and keep raising that bar.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Partner with strategists (who own the why and what) and our designers/editors to turn ideas into finished, on-brand assets fast.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Work at pace and volume without letting craft slip — you&#39;re comfortable shipping a lot and keeping it sharp.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Help shape the studio&#39;s visual identity and creative standards as we scale.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;&lt;strong&gt;What you&#39;ll bring&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;A strong portfolio of performance and/or brand creative — with a clear eye for art direction, composition, type and visual craft.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Real production experience: you can plan and run a shoot, direct talent, and take something from idea to finished asset yourself.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Hands-on editing/design ability — enough to set the standard, jump in, and unblock others (Premiere/After Effects, Figma/Adobe CS or similar).&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;A performance instinct: you understand social-native, direct-response creative and what makes an ad actually convert, not just look good.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;A bias for output and iteration — you ship, learn and ship again, without being precious.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Comfortable directing people (talent, crew, the bench) and collaborating closely with strategists and editors.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Why join Eucalyptus?&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Euc is also behind a growing family of digital healthcare clinics (&lt;a href=&quot;https://pilot.com.au/&quot;&gt;Pilot,&lt;/a&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;a href=&quot;http://www.kinfertility.com.au/&quot;&gt;Kin&lt;/a&gt;,&amp;nbsp;&lt;a href=&quot;http://skin.software/&quot;&gt;Software&lt;/a&gt;) across men’s health and well-being, fertility, and skincare.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Here’s what makes joining Euc unique:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;What’s next&lt;/strong&gt; - Our goal for the next three years is to support &lt;strong&gt;1 million patients globally&lt;/strong&gt; to live better for longer. We’re launching into new conditions, demographics, and geographies as we build a truly preventive healthcare ecosystem.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Build something world-changing&lt;/strong&gt; - We’re on the path to becoming the world’s largest international digital healthcare company. It will be challenging, fast-paced, and deeply rewarding.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Make real impact&lt;/strong&gt; - You will deliver work that directly shapes patient outcomes and scales evidence-based care across markets.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Accelerate your growth&lt;/strong&gt; - You will have high ownership, continuous feedback, and dedicated development support.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Join a motivated team&lt;/strong&gt; - You will collaborate with talented peers to solve complex clinical and operational problems at scale.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;What’s ahead in the UK&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Be an owner&lt;/strong&gt; – Your own stake in the business with our employee options program&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Invest in your growth&lt;/strong&gt; – Annual development budget plus 3 days of professional development leave&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Work flexibly&lt;/strong&gt; – Hybrid setup with 3 days a week in our Old Street office, designed for focus and collaboration&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Support your well-being&lt;/strong&gt; – Private health insurance through Vitality or opt for a monthly wellness allowance to spend on what matters most to you&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Take time off&lt;/strong&gt; – 25 days of holiday, enhanced parental leave and work from anywhere 3 weeks out of the year&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Join a connected team&lt;/strong&gt; – A vibrant office culture with regular socials, clubs, after-school sport, and seasonal events&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;em&gt;At Eucalyptus, we value individuals from all backgrounds, experiences, and perspectives, and we embrace the unique qualities each person brings. When you apply, please let us know of any reasonable adjustments you may need during the interview process.&lt;/em&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;div class=&quot;content-conclusion&quot;&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;em&gt;At Eucalyptus, we value individuals from all backgrounds, experiences, and perspectives, and we embrace the unique qualities each person brings. When you apply, please let us know of any reasonable adjustments you may need during the interview process. We use AI-assisted tools across our business to help our teams work more efficiently, including within our recruitment process. These tools support our team — all hiring decisions are made by real people, and every application is reviewed by a member of our recruitment team.&lt;/em&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;/div&gt;

