&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Design and build a standardised evaluation framework covering clinical interactions, health coach conversations, AI assistant conversations, PX support, and health insights&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Build and run services that monitor patient-facing conversations and automatically flag risky content for review and escalation&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Develop eval datasets, metrics, and thresholds with clinicians, coaches, and support leads — turning “what good looks like” into something measurable&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Own the technical integration between our AI assistants and our data models, making patient &amp;amp; business context available to assistants safely, and consistently&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Operate your systems in production: monitoring, alerting, and iterating as models and prompts evolve&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Own and automate guardrail updates based on internal and patient feedback from interactions with our third-party support tools&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Share results with the teams who own each workstream, and help them improve&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;About You&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;A degree in computer science, engineering, data science, or a related field — or equivalent practical experience&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Strong Python skills and the fundamentals to build reliable services, not just notebooks&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Hands-on experience with LLMs: prompt engineering, and ideally exposure to eval frameworks or LLM-as-judge approaches (coursework, internships, or personal projects all count)&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;A careful, safety-first mindset — you care about what an AI system says to a real patient, and you sweat the edge cases&lt;/li&gt;
