&lt;p&gt;As an Account Growth Manager, you&#39;ll operate in a hybrid Account Manager and Field Manager capacity, owning the growth strategy for a portfolio of consultative merchants. You&#39;ll combine commercial thinking with hands on relationship management, helping merchants maximise performance, increase product adoption and create exceptional customer experiences while identifying new opportunities to grow our partnerships.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h4&gt;What you&#39;ll own&lt;/h4&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Own the growth, retention and performance of a portfolio of strategic merchant partners, developing account plans that drive revenue, customer acquisition and long term success.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Build trusted relationships with stakeholders across merchant organisations, from frontline teams through to senior leaders.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Identify and execute growth opportunities that strengthen partnerships and deliver measurable commercial outcomes.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Negotiate commercial initiatives and partnership opportunities that create value for both Zip and our merchant partners.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Deliver face to face training, coaching and ongoing support to ensure merchants are confident, engaged and compliant when offering Zip solutions.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Conduct regular business reviews, sharing insights, performance trends and recommendations that help merchants achieve their goals.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Analyse merchant performance data to identify opportunities to improve sales, customer experience and product adoption.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Execute Best Practice Integration standards, ensuring Zip branding, customer messaging and in store experiences are optimised.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Partner closely with Business Development, Marketing, Product, Engineering, Legal, Sales Operations and Customer Experience teams to deliver great outcomes for merchants.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Act as the voice of the merchant by providing feedback that helps shape product improvements, commercial strategy and future opportunities.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Manage escalations effectively while maintaining strong governance, compliance and risk management across your portfolio.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Represent Zip professionally in the field, strengthening our brand and building lasting merchant relationships.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h4&gt;What you&#39;ll bring to the team&lt;/h4&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Zipsters work on a broad range of initiatives, and our skills and experiences all look a little different. What really matters to us is that you&#39;re a great fit with our four Values, and have a desire to learn and grow.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;So whether you meet some or all of the desirable attributes below, we&#39;d still love to hear from you.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience in Strategic Account Management, Key Account Management, Field Sales, Business Development or Merchant Growth.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;A proven track record of growing customer portfolios and building long term commercial partnerships.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Strong commercial acumen with an understanding of retail, payments, fintech or financial services.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Excellent relationship management, communication, negotiation and presentation skills.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;The ability to analyse data and translate insights into practical growth strategies.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience working with CRM platforms such as Salesforce.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Strong planning, organisation and time management skills with the ability to manage multiple priorities.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;A willingness to travel regularly and work flexibly to support merchant training and business needs.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;A mindset that embraces AI and new tools to adapt, learn and grow.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;An aptitude for identifying and managing risks. Whether you are a People Manager or an Individual Contributor, we are all leaders at Zip, therefore effective risk management is important to how we run our business and part of all our roles.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Our values in your DNA. Customer First, Own It, Stronger Together and Change the Game.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h4&gt;What you’ll get in return&lt;/h4&gt;
&lt;p&gt;As we write this next exciting chapter in our story, we will continue to move at pace and embrace change. For you, this might mean opportunities to learn new skills with hands-on experience, broader responsibilities, or the buzz of seeing your work impact customers faster.&amp;nbsp;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Zip is a place where you’ll get out exactly what you put in. When you join the team, we&#39;ll do our best to make sure you can be yourself and surround yourself with smart, friendly colleagues and leaders who have your back, so that you can make the big things happen.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Zipsters tell us these are just some of the best things about working here. You’ll also receive:&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;25 days paid leave annually, including birthday leave and quarterly wellbeing days&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;16 weeks paid parental leave for primary carers, and 4 weeks for supporting carers&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Family support policies including miscarriage bereavement leave and domestic violence leave&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Mental health and wellness initiatives, including $299 annual wellbeing allowance, free access for you and family members to our EAP service Sonder, discounted private health insurance, and great rates on fitness sessions through ClassPass&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;2 days paid volunteering leave per year&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Access to the Flare Benefits Hub and Novated Leasing for savings across lifestyle, essentials and wellbeing&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Fee-free Zip products, and discounts with Zip merchant partners (AU)&amp;nbsp;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Team social events, epic offices, free breakfast daily, and weekly free lunches (Sydney and Melbourne)&amp;nbsp;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h4&gt;Be a part of a team that reflects the diversity of our customers&lt;/h4&gt;
&lt;p&gt;We pride ourselves on being a workplace that provides equal opportunities to people of all ages, cultural backgrounds, sexual orientations, gender identities, abilities, veteran status, and everything else that makes you unique.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Equally, we’re committed to ensuring our recruitment processes are accessible and inclusive. Please let us know If there are any adjustments that need to be made to ensure you have a fair and equitable experience.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h4&gt;And finally…get to know us&lt;/h4&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Zip Co Limited (ASX: ZIP) is a digital financial services company, offering innovative, people-centred products that bring customers and merchants together.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Operating in two core markets - Australia and the US, Zip offers point-of-sale credit and digital payment services, connecting millions of customers with its global network of tens of thousands of merchants.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;We’re proud to be a values-led business and our values - Customer First, Own it, Stronger Together and Change the Game - guide us in everything we do.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;#LI-Hybrid&lt;/p&gt;

aaf98f19-a719-5d81-8970-9ba221f56fec.original_description:
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Legal Expertise: J.D. from an accredited law school, active membership in at least one U.S. state bar in good standing, and 12+ years of corporate law experience within a nationally recognized law firm and/or sophisticated in-house legal team.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;M&amp;amp;A Leadership: Extensive experience leading complex mergers, acquisitions, divestitures, and strategic transactions, with end-to-end ownership from signing through post-closing integration.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;NYC Hybrid Flexibility: Opportunity to work hybrid from our New York City office, combining in-person collaboration with flexibility.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Start your adventure with Zip&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;p&gt;We’re seeking an experienced and strategic Assistant General Counsel to join Zip’s Legal team, serving as a senior subject-matter expert across our corporate, financing, securities and strategic transaction activities. This is a highly visible role partnering with executive leadership, Finance, Group Treasury, Investor Relations, Strategy and cross-functional stakeholders to provide practical legal guidance that enables business growth while appropriately managing legal risk.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;As a trusted legal advisor, you’ll play a lead role in sophisticated corporate transactions, advise on securities and disclosure matters, support complex financing initiatives, and help shape scalable legal processes that support Zip’s continued growth. You’ll combine exceptional legal judgment with strong commercial acumen to navigate complex business challenges in a fast-paced, collaborative environment.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;This is a remote-first role, with occasional in-person team gatherings and the option to work from our Manhattan office.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Interesting problems you’ll get to solve&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Primary legal lead for mergers, acquisitions, divestitures, strategic partnerships, and other corporate development initiatives from transaction structuring through post-closing integration.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Primary legal lead for complex financing activities, including warehouse financing arrangements, receivables financing structures, securitizations, credit facilities, capital markets transactions, guarantees, and liquidity initiatives.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Advise on U.S. securities law compliance and public company disclosure obligations, including periodic reporting, registration statements, and other filings applicable to public company or foreign private issuer frameworks.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Support the Company&#39;s corporate governance framework by preparing Board and committee materials, resolutions, governance policies, and related corporate records, while advising on governance matters and evolving best practices.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Partner with executive leadership to provide strategic legal counsel on securities laws, insider trading compliance, corporate governance, and public company disclosure requirements.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Coordinate cross-functional stakeholders and manage outside counsel throughout all phases of strategic transactions while driving efficient execution.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Identify legal risks and develop practical, commercially focused solutions that enable business objectives while appropriately managing legal risk.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Develop scalable legal processes, templates, governance practices, and operational efficiencies that support a growing and evolving legal function.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Leverage AI-assisted legal tools to enhance legal workflows, evaluate AI-enabled work products, and advise stakeholders on AI governance, privacy considerations, and legal risks associated with emerging technologies.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Mentor junior legal professionals and contribute to the continued development of a collaborative, high-performing legal team.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;&lt;strong&gt;What you’ll bring to the team&amp;nbsp;&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Juris Doctor (J.D.) from an accredited law school and active membership in at least one U.S. state bar in good standing.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;12+ years of experience in corporate law, including significant experience at a nationally recognized law firm and/or a sophisticated in-house legal department.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Extensive M&amp;amp;A experience leading complex mergers, acquisitions, divestitures, and strategic transactions from signing through post-closing integration.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Deep finance expertise supporting structured finance and corporate finance transactions, including warehouse financing, receivables financing, securitizations, credit facilities, and capital markets transactions.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Strong securities law knowledge, including experience supporting public company or foreign private issuer reporting frameworks and advising on disclosure obligations, Form 20-F, Form 6-K, earnings releases, and investor communications.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Executive partnership with a demonstrated ability to advise senior leadership on complex legal, governance, and strategic business matters.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;AI fluency with the ability to leverage and critically evaluate AI-generated legal work product, understand AI governance and privacy considerations, identify legal risks associated with responsible AI use, and apply sound judgment when incorporating AI into legal workflows.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Commercial judgment with a proven ability to independently manage multiple high-priority matters while balancing legal risk with business objectives.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Cross-functional leadership with experience managing outside counsel and partnering effectively across Legal, Finance, Treasury, Investor Relations, and Corporate Development.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Operational excellence demonstrated through improving legal operations, governance processes, templates, or scalable legal frameworks within a fast-paced environment.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Preferred: Experience as in-house counsel at a public fintech, financial services, or payments company, or equivalent advisory experience at a top-tier law firm.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;What you’ll get in return&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Zip is a place where you&#39;ll get out what you put in. The newness of our sector means we need to move at pace and embrace change, and our promise to you when you join the team is that you&#39;ll feel empowered and trusted to make big things happen quickly.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;We want you to feel welcome and as though you have the support to be yourself, and care for yourself at work. Because it&#39;s important to us that you make the most of the opportunities you&#39;ll get to grow your skills and your career, and be surrounded by smart, friendly people and leaders that have your back.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;We think these are some of the best things about being a Zipster. We will also offer you:&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Flexible working culture&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Incentive programs&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Unlimited PTO&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Generous paid parental leave&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Leading family support policies&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Company-sponsored 401k match&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Learning and wellness subscription stipend&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Beautiful Union Square office with a casual dress code&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Industry-leading, employer-sponsored insurance for you and your dependents, with several 100% Zip-covered choices available&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Zip is committed to a straightforward and transparent pay structure. The actual base salary will be determined by various individualized factors, including job-related knowledge, skills, experience, location, internal equity, as well as other objective business considerations.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;The annual base Pay Range for this position is $248k – $260k. This range reflects our US national compensation band (USN). Additional premium percentages may apply based on our tiered premium strategy.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Subject to those same considerations, the total compensation package for this position may also include other elements, including a bonus and/or equity awards, in addition to a full range of medical, financial, and/or other benefits.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;If hired, employees will be in an &quot;at-will&quot; position and the Company reserves the right to modify base salary (as well as any other discretionary payment or compensation or benefit program) at any time, including for reasons related to individual performance, Company or individual department/team performance, and market factors.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Be a part of a team that reflects the diversity of our customers&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;We pride ourselves on being a workplace that provides equal opportunities to people of all ages, cultural backgrounds, sexual orientations, gender identities, abilities, veteran status, and everything else that makes you unique.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Equally, we&#39;re committed to ensuring our recruitment processes are accessible and inclusive. Please let us know if there are any adjustments that need to be made to ensure you have a fair and equitable experience.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;And finally…get to know us&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Zip Co Limited (ASX: ZIP) is a digital financial services company, offering innovative, people-centered products.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Operating in two core markets - Australia and New Zealand (ANZ) and the US, Zip offers access to point-of-sale credit and digital payment services, connecting millions of customers with its global network of tens of thousands of merchants.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;We’re proud to be a values-led business and our values - Customer First, Own it, Stronger Together and Change the Game - guide us in everything we do.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;em&gt;I acknowledge by clicking &quot;Submit Application&quot;, that the information provided is true and correct. I also understand that any willful dishonesty may render for refusal of this application or immediate termination of employment. By providing your information, you acknowledge that you have read our &lt;/em&gt;&lt;a href=&quot;https://zip.co/careers/us-candidate-privacy-notice&quot;&gt;&lt;em&gt;Zip Applicant and Candidate Privacy Notice&lt;/em&gt;&lt;/a&gt;&lt;em&gt; and authorize Zip to process your data subject to those terms &lt;/em&gt;&lt;strong&gt;&lt;em&gt;Zip participates in the federal government’s E-Verify program&lt;/em&gt;&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;a href=&quot;https://rebrand.ly/check-zip-out&quot;&gt;&lt;strong&gt;&lt;em&gt;Before you apply, give Zip a try &amp;nbsp; -&amp;gt; rebrand.ly/check-zip-out&lt;/em&gt;&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;We are a proud 2025 Circle Back initiative employer and will respond to every applicant.&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;

