&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Partner closely with the Chair to support the efficient and effective operation of the Board and its Committees.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Act as a key connection point between the Board and Group Executive Team, coordinating agendas, Board and Committee papers, policies and meeting requirements.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Attend Board and Committee meetings, ensuring minutes accurately capture key discussions and decisions and that agreed actions are communicated, followed through and completed.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Plan and facilitate Board strategy sessions, workshops, director inductions, ongoing education and compliance training.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Own the Board and Board Committee calendars and support the ongoing maintenance of charters and governance frameworks.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Organise and manage shareholder meetings, including Zip’s Annual General Meeting.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Provide guidance on Zip’s governance policies, procedures and frameworks, including the operation of delegated authorities.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Partner with Legal Counsel to support compliance with ASX reporting requirements and applicable corporate governance obligations.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Oversee required ASIC forms and returns, ensuring obligations are completed accurately and within prescribed timeframes.&lt;/li&gt;
