&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Start your adventure with Zip&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;p&gt;With the merchant and consumer growth ambitions at Zip, we are looking for a &lt;strong&gt;Director, Strategic Partnerships&lt;/strong&gt; who will own, grow, and manage our strategic partnerships in the US. As the Director, Strategic Partnerships, you will have a deep understanding of the AI and technology partnership landscape and bring strong commercial, strategic, and relationship management skills.&amp;nbsp;This role sits at the core of the organization. You will partner closely with internal and external executives, and work cross-functionally with product, sales, marketing, risk, data, and finance teams to design and execute high-impact partnership strategies.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;The key goals for this role are to:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;br&gt;a) Define Zip&#39;s long-term AI, platform, and ecosystem strategy and identify new growth vectors capable of driving material enterprise value.&lt;br&gt;b) Shape executive decision-making on build/buy/partner strategies across merchant, consumer, and platform ecosystems.&lt;br&gt;c) Identify, incubate, and commercialize transformational partnerships, platform bets, and strategic investments that create durable competitive advantage.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;You will focus on core partners including AI leaders (e.g., OpenAI, Anthropic), Amazon, Meta, Adobe, and other strategic technology platforms, and operate as a visible leader and subject-matter expert on AI and platform partnerships across Zip US.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Interesting problems you’ll get to solve&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Develop a deep understanding of the AI, platform &amp;amp; technology landscape to create new opportunities&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Pull together a consolidated view of trends across AI, cloud, advertising, and commerce platforms, and translate insights into product, commercial, and sales recommendations&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Complete deep dives on new opportunities across key verticals (e.g., retail, eCommerce, marketplaces) and distribution channels tied to core partners like OpenAI, Anthropic, Amazon, Meta, and Adobe&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Be extremely proficient in PowerPoint, Excel, and Salesforce to model scenarios, structure narratives, and manage partner pipeline and performance&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Leverage AI tools to surface partnership insights, automate reporting, and identify revenue optimization opportunities across AI and platform partners (e.g., AI-assisted analysis of partner performance, GTM content generation, and risk/opportunity scanning)&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Educate executives and sales teams on the AI and platform ecosystem, competitive landscape, and partnership opportunities through structured, data-backed storytelling&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Manage and grow relationships with strategic AI and technology partners to increase market share&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Develop growth strategy and clear plans for core partners including AI leaders (OpenAI, Anthropic), commerce platforms (Amazon), social platforms (Meta), and creative/experience platforms (Adobe)&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Track performance metrics with these strategic partners, ensuring commercial terms are optimized and operationalized&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Drive revenue growth and cost optimization by developing joint solutions, integrations, and programs that leverage these platforms to acquire and engage merchants and consumers&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Work with product teams to lead RFPs and drive the right product and commercial outcomes for Zip; understand partner roadmaps and how Zip can leverage upcoming capabilities ahead of competitors&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Collaborate with sales and marketing to develop high-impact co-marketing, marketplace, and distribution initiatives that help both the partner and Zip succeed&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Lead regular education, relationship-building, and knowledge-sharing between partner teams and Zip teams, becoming a thought leader in AI and strategic platform partnerships for Zip&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Lead internal alignment, governance, and execution&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Regularly align with regional and global counterparts to understand intra-region trends and best practices, and apply them to the US market&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Provide clear, recurring updates on partnerships, pipeline, opportunities, and risks to key regional stakeholders and executive sponsors&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Ensure strong processes, operating rhythms, and governance are built and followed to set up all partnerships and merchants for success&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Track and analyse partner performance (merchant growth, transaction volume, unit economics, activation/adoption of AI or platform features) and propose strategic courses of action, experiments, and improvements&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Impact and collaboration&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;strong&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;/strong&gt; The &lt;strong&gt;Director, Strategic Partnerships&lt;/strong&gt; will be a key leader within the Partnerships team, driving critical initiatives across:&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;AI &amp;amp; Platform Strategy:&lt;/strong&gt; Develop strategy and approach to leverage AI and key platforms (OpenAI, Anthropic, Amazon, Meta, Adobe, and others) to enhance Zip’s products, economics, and customer experiences.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Partnership Enablement:&lt;/strong&gt; Assess and negotiate global and regional deals with partners and channels to drive revenue via new SMB and Enterprise merchant acquisition.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Partnership Management:&lt;/strong&gt; Own and track merchant and partner KPIs with our strategic partners, ensuring Zip achieves its growth, profitability, and customer experience goals through these platforms.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;&lt;strong&gt;What you’ll bring to the team&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Proven industry or consulting experience&lt;/strong&gt; – Preferably 10+ years in strategy, partnerships, consulting, or technology business development, with a strong track record of managing and growing relationships with AI or platform partners.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Analytical &amp;amp; financial acumen&lt;/strong&gt; – Advanced Excel and financial modeling skills, strong comfort with data-driven decision-making, and a track record of optimizing commercial outcomes at scale&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Demonstrated use of AI in your role&lt;/strong&gt; – Experience using AI tools (e.g., ChatGPT, Notion AI, Salesforce Einstein, or similar) to improve decision-making, efficiency, GTM execution, or partner engagement&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Salesforce &amp;amp; GTM execution&lt;/strong&gt; – Proven ability to track complex deals, manage partner pipelines, operationalize co-selling motions, and execute go-to-market strategies with sales and marketing teams&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Negotiation &amp;amp; influence&lt;/strong&gt; – Experience leading complex deal cycles end-to-end, collaborating cross-functionally, and influencing senior stakeholders internally and externally&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Consulting experience helpful&lt;/strong&gt; – Experience at a top-tier consulting firm (e.g., Deloitte, McKinsey, BCG, Bain) or in a similarly rigorous strategic environment is a plus&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Results-driven &amp;amp; innovative&lt;/strong&gt; – Demonstrated success in driving revenue growth, scaling or transforming partnership programs, and solving problems creatively in ambiguous environments&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Ability to process complex information, analyse options, and think “outside the box” to deliver outcomes&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Ability to collaborate with, influence, and persuade others using structured, logical thinking and clear communication&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Strong customer-first ethic and a results-orientated mindset with a track record to prove it&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Alignment with Zip’s values: Customer First, Own It, Stronger Together, and Change the Game in how you lead, execute, and build partnerships&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;&lt;strong&gt;What you’ll get in return&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Flexible working culture&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Incentive programs&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Unlimited PTO&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Generous paid parental leave&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Leading family support policies&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Company-sponsored 401k match&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Learning and wellness subscription stipend&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Beautiful Union Square office with a casual dress code&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Industry-leading, employer-sponsored insurance for you and your dependents, with several 100% Zip-covered choices available&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Zip is committed to a straightforward and transparent pay structure. The actual base salary will be determined by various individualized factors, including job-related knowledge, skills, experience, location, internal equity, as well as other objective business considerations.&lt;/p&gt;
