5f18c632-b509-5b01-b37b-e8a2f638a297.original_description:
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Track record of leading loan origination and new customer onboarding, optimizing approval rates while mitigating fraud and credit risk&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Strong analytical and data fluency with experience using business metrics to drive product strategy and prioritization&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience with different AI tools and techniques to accelerate personal and/or squad productivity&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Remote-first opportunity for US-based employees with the option to work in-person out of our Manhattan office&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Start your adventure with Zip&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;We are seeking a collaborative, data-driven &lt;strong&gt;Senior Technical Product Manager – Underwriting Platform&lt;/strong&gt; to manage lead and scale the technology powering our customer onboarding and underwriting platform. In this role, you will drive platform capabilities to maximize loan approval rates, effectively aligning technical solutions with risk strategies and business goals.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;The ideal candidate will manage the roadmap responsible for driving new customer acquisition and activation, optimizing decisioning, and integrating advanced identity and credit data services.&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;The Product organization at Zip focuses on delivering seamless and innovative financial experiences that support millions of customers. Our teams move quickly, operate with high ownership, and solve complex problems collaboratively. We value a self-starter mindset, curiosity, customer obsession, and strong execution.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Interesting problems you’ll solve&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Define and execute platform strategies that drive measurable outcomes across sign-up, loan approvals, and activation while balancing risk.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Partner closely with Engineering, Credit, and Fraud teams to build scalable, compliant, and performant onboarding and lending platform capabilities.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Evaluate and implement AI-enabled product capabilities, workflows, and or automation opportunities that improve customer onboarding experiences and operational efficiency&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Collaborate with Engineering and Risk to deliver low-code platform features that accelerate business responsiveness to changing business, risk, and regulatory requirementsenvironmental and compliance landscapes.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;What you’ll bring to the team&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;6+ years of Product Management experience, including experience supporting fintech, payments, lending, or financial services platforms&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Proven experience owning onboarding, activation, or growth-focused product initiatives with measurable business impact&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Strong technical fluency with the ability to collaborate effectively with Engineering teams on APIs, platform architecture, and technical tradeoffs&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Demonstrated ability to use data, experimentation, and business metrics to inform prioritization and product decisions&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Strong understanding of experimentation methodologies including A/B testing, cohort analysis, and growth optimization frameworks&lt;/li&gt;
